eated in prior task)\n      - CLAUDE.md (differential testing pattern, BuildBinary usage, LookPath skip convention)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct, RunDiffTests function)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/pathchk/pathchk_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests comparing Go pathchk against gpathchk reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Write differential tests covering srd103-pathchk R2.1 -- test cases exercise the behavior specified in that requirement\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Write differential tests covering srd103-pathchk R2.2 -- test cases exercise the behavior specified in that requirement\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Write differential tests covering srd103-pathchk R2.3 -- test cases exercise the behavior specified in that requirement\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \\\".\\\") to compile the Go binary and exec.LookPath(\\\"gpathchk\\\") for the reference binary\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Call t.Skip if gpathchk is not found in PATH -- tests must pass on machines without Homebrew GNU binaries\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Define tests as []testutils.DiffTest and run via testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Set LC_ALL=C in test environment to ensure consistent behavior between Go and GNU binaries\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/pathchk/... -count=1 passes (or skips gracefully if gpathchk not found)\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Tests cover all behavior specified in srd103-pathchk R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 with concrete inputs and expected outcomes\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"TestDiff function follows the differential testing pattern from CLAUDE.md\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"cmd/test: implement srd104 R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_